# Rule Governance

## Purpose

Keep rules concise and non-duplicative by assigning a single primary owner file per topic.

## Topic owners

- **Architecture owner:** `project-architecture.mdc` (system shape and cross-layer boundaries)
- **Workflow owner:** `project-workflow.mdc` (upload/analyze/build/deploy user flow)
- **Runtime safety owner:** `project-runtime-safety.mdc` (execution constraints and deploy/runtime semantics)
- **Testing owner:** `testing-conventions.mdc` (quality gates and test expectations)
- **Backend implementation owners:** `backend-*.mdc` files (router/infrastructure/plugin/python specifics)
- **Frontend implementation owners:** `frontend-*.mdc` + `results-and-monitoring.mdc`
- **Privacy owner:** `research-privacy.mdc`
- **DevOps owner:** `docker-and-devops.mdc`

## De-duplication policy

- Put canonical statements in the owner file and keep references elsewhere short.
- When two rules overlap, prefer cross-reference instead of repeating detailed guidance.
- Use "current behavior" wording when documenting code-backed behavior that may change later.

## When to apply

- Apply this governance rule whenever adding/updating rule files.
- If a rule grows broad or duplicates another rule, split or trim it before adding new guidance.
